{
  "dom_id": "step-q9749",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a series $\\frac{1}{2}+2+8+\u22ef?$",
  "worked_solution": "Note that $\\frac{1}{2}+2+8+\u22ef$ is the sum of a geometric series since the ratio of any two consecutive terms is constant.\n\nFirst, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case ${a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $r=4.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}(1-{4}^{N})}{-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{3}\\cdot ({4}^{N}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}({4}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
